Subject: [PATCH 01798/11362] [outer-loop] #2 circularity/oracle-distinctness
 guard (operator 2+3+1)

Turns tonight's two manual catches (v2 invalid null; capstone flipping the DiffusionGemma
gate to MET on a circular code win) into a mechanical guard. The loop's fabrication gate
caught fakes but not over-INTERPRETATION (circular win -> 'moat proven').

- adversarial_verify.py: new check_circular_moat_overclaim -> CIRCULAR_MOAT_OVERCLAIM.
  CRITICAL when an artifact flips a gate / headlines a moat while verifier_is_oracle is
  true or undeclared (quarantines the over-claim); WARN when a moat/efficiency claim omits
  or sets verifier_is_oracle=true (surfaces circularity, keeps the result).
- CLAUDE.md: new 'Circularity / Oracle-Distinctness Discipline' -- every verifier-value/
  moat claim declares verifier_is_oracle; circular (verifier==oracle) wins are
  execution_grounded results, NOT headline/gate-eligible; only oracle-distinct (learned/
  energy) wins are. The deep claim stays the open frontier.
- exp4183 .387 capstone: completes 'fix the MET' -- the honest_verdict STRING still said
  moat_PROVEN/diffusiongemma_MET (structured fields were already corrected); now reads
  moat_CIRCULAR_execution_only / diffusiongemma_STILL_PENDING (original preserved).

